    "created_at": "2025-11-10T23:45:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-10T23:45:06Z",
    "body": "I addressed this at length in https://github.com/w3c/aria/issues/2663. Please see that issue for more details, but in short, the problem is that there is no \"default role\" for quite a few element types; e.g. `<section>`. The role has to be determined based on other factors currently handled by the accessibility engine. You could just choose one, but there's no way to be sure that what you chose was the author's intent, so you're potentially lying to the API consumer.",
